  "pages": [
    {
      "page_idx": 4,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "index": 0,
          "bbox": [
            0.099,
            0.104,
            0.138,
            0.119
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "206"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "header",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.782,
            0.104,
            0.9,
            0.121
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "MATHEMATICS"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.139,
            0.901,
            0.178
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Are the events E and F in the example above elementary events? No, they are "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "not",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " because the event E has 2 outcomes and the event F has 4 outcomes."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.097,
            0.185,
            0.51,
            0.204
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Remarks :",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " From Example 1, we note that"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.249,
            0.213,
            0.897,
            0.254
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_4_equation_4.jpg",
          "content": "\\mathrm { P ( E )   +   P ( F )   =   \\frac { 1 } { 2 }   +   \\frac { 1 } { 2 }   =   1 }\\tag{1}"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.259,
            0.772,
            0.279
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "where E is the event ‘getting a head’ and F is the event ‘getting a tail’."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.146,
            0.285,
            0.562,
            0.305
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "From (i) and (ii) of Example 3, we also get"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.25,
            0.317,
            0.896,
            0.358
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_4_equation_7.jpg",
          "content": "\\mathrm { P ( E ) + P ( F ) = } { \\frac { 1 } { 3 } } + { \\frac { 2 } { 3 } } = 1\\tag{2}"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.369,
            0.896,
            0.389
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "where E is the event ‘getting a number "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "{ > } 4 ^ { \\circ }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and F is the event ‘getting a number "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\leq 4 ^ { \\circ }"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.396,
            0.901,
            0.434
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Note that getting a number not greater than 4 is same as getting a number less than or equal to 4, and vice versa."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.098,
            0.441,
            0.902,
            0.485
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "In (1) and (2) above, is F not the same as ‘not "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathrm { E } ^ { \\prime } ?"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Yes, it is. We denote the event ‘not "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathrm { E ^ { \\prime } }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " by "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\overline { { \\overline { { \\mathrm { E } } } } }"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.097,
            0.488,
            0.413,
            0.508
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "So, P(E) + P(not E) = 1"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.516,
            0.772,
            0.538
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "i.e., "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathrm{P}(\\mathrm{E}) + \\mathrm{P}(\\overline{\\mathrm{E}}) \\equiv 1;"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " which gives us P( E ) = 1 – P(E)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.146,
            0.544,
            0.58,
            0.564
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "In general, it is true that for an event "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathbf { E } _ { z }"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.301,
            0.571,
            0.487,
            0.592
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_4_equation_14.jpg",
          "content": "\\mathbf{P}(\\mathbf{E}) = \\mathbf{1} - \\mathbf{P}(\\mathbf{E})"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.6,
            0.899,
            0.647
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The event "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\overline { \\mathrm { E } }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " , representing ‘not E’, is called the "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "complement",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " of the event E. We also say that E and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\overline { { \\overline { { \\mathrm { E } } } } }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " are "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "complementary",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " events."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.147,
            0.653,
            0.901,
            0.674
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Before proceeding further, let us try to find the answers to the following questions:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.118,
            0.679,
            0.831,
            0.699
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(i) What is the probability of getting a number 8 in a single throw of a die?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 18,
          "bbox": [
            0.098,
            0.706,
            0.901,
            0.753
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(ii) What is the probability of getting a number less than 7 in a single throw of a die? "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Let us answer (i) :",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 19,
          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.762,
            0.902,
            0.847
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We know that there are only six possible outcomes in a single throw of a die. These outcomes are 1, 2, 3, 4, 5 and 6. Since no face of the die is marked 8, so there is no outcome favourable to 8, i.e., the number of such outcomes is zero. In other words, getting 8 in a single throw of a die, is impossible."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 20,
          "bbox": [
            0.098,
            0.868,
            0.135,
            0.887
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "So,"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 21,
          "bbox": [
            0.249,
            0.855,
            0.464,
            0.896
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_4_equation_21.jpg",
          "content": "\\mathrm{P}(\\mathrm{getting}\\ 8)=\\frac{0}{6}=0"
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "index": 22,
          "bbox": [
            0.435,
            0.966,
            0.563,
            0.983
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Reprint 2026-27"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
